      "title": "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c183f60b-3002-5e1a-9704-5c887367ceab",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x+90^\\circ)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.\n\n$\\sin(x+90^\\circ)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x+90^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 90^\\circ+\\cos x\\sin 90^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)+\\cos x\\cdot\\left(1\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "aebe5936-6055-5e6c-8f3e-2cd780ebc777",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
